id: pm-01kwb2
title: Stabilize alias clear/prune race verification under monolithic release coverage
description: "Operator release 42759813393 on merged baf182d564 passed all 12365 assertions but exact coverage missed the return at src/sdk/telemetry.ts:567. The competing-clear fixture holds the telemetry lock while coordinating the peer; the permitted 250 ms SDK lock refusal can bypass the re-read branch under whole-suite load while every assertion still passes. Coordinate the peer state transition before real SDK lock admission so the guard is tested deterministically without changing production behavior or lock budgets."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-10T05:50:52.473Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-10T07:12:30.714Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-10T07:12:29.424Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-10T07:12:29.424Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Use real filesystem and mutex behavior with deterministic peer ordering rather than elapsed-time admission; A removed clear guard fails the behavioral regression and the real guard branch is covered under unchanged global thresholds; Keep the 250 ms production wait and shipped SDK behavior unchanged
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Replaced timing-dependent held-lock scheduling with real mutex-backed peer transitions and an explicit locked-operation admission assertion. Kept SDK production code and lock budgets unchanged.
expected_result: Both cleared and already-pruned peer states exercise the locked re-read; removing the clear-safe guard must recreate a cleared file and fail the test.
actual_result: "All 31 linked telemetry tests pass; a removed-guard isolated control fails the cleared-file case as intended. Complete monolithic coverage covers every line, statement, function and branch across 843 source files with zero deficits, including the previously missing SDK guard."
